  "notes": "ずきずき is an onomatopoeia specifically for throbbing, pulsating pain. The pain comes in waves, often synchronized with the heartbeat.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {頭|あたま}がずきずきする: head is throbbing\n- {歯|は}がずきずきする: tooth is throbbing\n- {傷|きず}がずきずき{痛|いた}む: the wound throbs with pain\n- ずきずきした{痛|いた}み: throbbing pain\n\nCONTRAST WITH OTHER PAIN WORDS:\n- ちくちく: pricking, stinging pain (needles, thorns)\n- ひりひり: burning, smarting pain (sunburn, raw skin)\n- きりきり: sharp, twisting pain (stomach)\n- がんがん: pounding pain (intense headache)\n- しくしく: dull, persistent ache (stomach)",
